course: dictionary
lesson: 518
title: Assume, don't assume
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To assume something is to think it is true without checking or having proof. «I assume you are hungry, so I have made a sandwich.» The speaker has not asked. They are guessing from what seems likely.
explain: Assume has other meanings too. «She assumed the role of captain» means she took on the job. «The cat assumed a sleepy pose» means the cat took up a sleepy position. Look at the words around assume to find which meaning fits.
explain: Assuming can cause trouble between friends. «When friends whisper and stop as you walk over, the worried brain fills the gap with the worst story.» Asking is usually better than assuming, because asking finds out what is really true.
fact: Assume is a verb. Its forms are assume, assumes, assumed and assuming.
fact: «Assume» can mean to think something is true without proof.
fact: «Assume responsibility» means to take on a job or duty.
fact: Useful phrases include «I assume that…», «assuming that…» and «don't assume».
fact: In maths and science, you may assume something to solve a problem, and you should say what you assumed.
exercise: «I assume you are tired after the match.» What does assume mean here? | Take a job on | *Think something is true without checking | Hold something very tightly | Ask a question politely
exercise: «She assumed the role of captain.» What does assumed mean here? | *Took on the job | Hid from the job | Asked for the job back | Forgot the job
exercise: Why is asking better than assuming when friends whisper? | Asking makes friends angry | Assuming is always right | Whispering means a fight is coming | *Asking finds out what is really true
test: «The cat assumed a sleepy pose.» What does assumed mean here? | *Took up a position | Ran away | Fell asleep at once | Chased a mouse
test: Which phrase means to take on a duty? | *assume responsibility | I assume that | assuming that | don't assume
exam: Jo says «Don't assume Sam is angry; ask him.» What is the best advice? | *Ask Sam what he really feels | Decide he is angry and avoid him | Stop speaking to Sam for ever | Assume he is angry and tell others
